= Norman Tebbit

Secretary of State for Employment. A former airline pilot and union official, he enjoys a fight, and Labour MPs call him "the Chingford Skinhead".

- @tebbit_act
- @on_your_bike
- @root: Return

@tebbit_act
title: Fast-track a new Employment Act
subtitle: Union power falls sharply.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; union_power -= 12; employment_acts += 1; strike_wave += 1; wet_dissent += 4; dry_dissent -= 3

Tebbit's Act narrows the definition of a lawful trade dispute and outlaws the closed shop unless a large majority of workers vote for it.

@on_your_bike
title: "On your bike"
subtitle: A conference speech on unemployment.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; right_dissent -= 5; dry_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 3; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent) if unemployment < 10; c2_con -= 1 if unemployment >= 10

Tebbit tells the conference that his unemployed father didn't riot in the 1930s: "He got on his bike and looked for work." [? if unemployment >= 10 : With unemployment at [+ unemployment_2 +]%, many people take it as an insult. ?]
